  "Question": "Let \\(n=x-y^{x-y}.\\) Find \\(n\\) when \\(x=2\\) and \\(y=-2.\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-14\\)",
    "B": "\\(0\\)",
    "C": "\\(1\\)",
    "D": "\\(18\\)",
    "E": "\\(256\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "First compute the exponent:\n\\[\nx-y=2-(-2)=4.\n\\]\nKeep parentheses around the negative value substituted for the base \\(y\\). Then\n\\[\nn=2-(-2)^4=2-16=-14.\n\\]\nThus \\(n=-14\\), choice A.",
